# Rust Patterns

**Borrow checker + `self.errors`:** Do not use `.ok_or_else(|| { self.errors.push(...) })`—the closure borrows `self`. Use `match` and return `Err(())`, or clone needed values before pushing.

```rust
// ✅ DO
let token = match self.peek() {
    Some(t) => t,
    None => { self.errors.push(ParseError::eof("expression")); return Err(()); }
};
```

**`Range<T>`:** Not `Copy`; use `.clone()` when converting `token.span` to `Span`.

**Before depending on types:** Read the real type definitions. Avoid assuming (e.g. `Token<'a>` when `Token` owns data).
